{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How Dotify is put together."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Dotify is a single Swift Package Manager executable built with SwiftUI and AppKit. It has three windows and two ways","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of talking to Spotify.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["            ┌──────────────── AppModel (shared state) ────────────────┐","            │                                                          │","  Spotify desktop app ◀─AppleScript─ SpotifyController ─▶ PanelController ─▶ player window","                                          │","                                          └─track changes─▶ LibraryStore ─▶ search window","                                                               ▲","  Spotify Web API ◀── SpotifyAPI ◀── SpotifyAuth (PKCE)        │","                         ▲                                     │","                         └──────────────── DeviceStore ─▶ speaker window","                                              ▲","                     CoreAudio · IOBluetooth · Bonjour"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"text":"Playback: AppleScript","type":"heading","anchor":"Playback-AppleScript","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/SpotifyController","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" polls the Spotify desktop app once a second through ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/ScriptRunner","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". It also refreshes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"immediately when Spotify posts its ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.spotify.client.PlaybackStateChanged","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" distributed notification. Scripts run on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one serial queue and are compiled once.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Between polls, the playback position is interpolated locally so progress bars move smoothly. After a local change,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such as seeking or changing volume, polled values are ignored for a moment so the UI doesn’t snap back.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Commands such as play\/pause, next, seek, volume, shuffle and ","type":"text"},{"code":"play track <uri>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are one-line AppleScript calls. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"controller checks whether Spotify is running first, because addressing it would otherwise launch it.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Web API: sign-in and requests","type":"heading","anchor":"Web-API-sign-in-and-requests","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/SpotifyAuth","type":"reference"},{"text":" implements Authorization Code with PKCE. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/LoopbackServer","type":"reference"},{"text":" accepts exactly one ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/callback","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" request on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"127.0.0.1:43821","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" using Network.framework. The refresh token lives in the Keychain via ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/Keychain","type":"reference"},{"text":". Access tokens are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"kept in memory and refreshed on demand, with concurrent callers sharing one refresh.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/SpotifyAPI","type":"reference"},{"text":" is a thin client that retries once after a 401 with a fresh token, and maps Spotify’s JSON into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/MediaItem","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/ConnectDevice","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Search and history","type":"heading","anchor":"Search-and-history","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/LibraryStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" owns the query, the multi-select ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/MediaKind","type":"reference"},{"text":" filters, debounced search results and Recently Played.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Recently Played merges Spotify’s history with a local history that ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/SpotifyController","type":"reference"},{"text":" feeds through its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"onTrackChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" callback. The local history is the only source of podcast episodes.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Speakers","type":"heading","anchor":"Speakers","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/DeviceStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" combines four sources:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/AudioOutputs"},{"text":": CoreAudio outputs and the default output device, with a listener for changes.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/BluetoothAudio","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": paired audio-class devices from IOBluetooth, connected with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"openConnection()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/AirPlayBrowser","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"_airplay._tcp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_sonos._tcp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" Bonjour browsing, to list AirPlay receivers and label Sonos rooms.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/SpotifyAPI"},{"text":": Spotify Connect devices and playback transfer.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Player-window","level":2,"text":"Player window","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/PanelController"},{"text":" owns the borderless, non-activating ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/PlayerPanel","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". It reacts to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/Preferences","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/PanelState"},{"text":" (hover, focus, toolbar):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It resizes for layout changes, keeping the top-left corner fixed.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It adds or removes the toolbar strip using ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/PanelGeometry","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". The strip goes on the top edge, or the bottom if there’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"no room above, and is removed from the same edge, so the player never drifts.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It fades the window to the idle opacity when the player is neither hovered nor focused."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It handles keyboard shortcuts.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/RootView"},{"type":"text","text":" picks the layout view and stacks "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/PlayerToolbar","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" on the correct edge.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Persistence","type":"heading","anchor":"Persistence","level":2},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Where"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"UserDefaults (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"local.dotify"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Layout, opacity, idle opacity, toggles, panel position, window frames, Client ID, granted scopes, filters, local history","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keychain (service ","type":"text"},{"code":"local.dotify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Spotify refresh token","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"text":"Testing","type":"heading","anchor":"Testing","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"swift test","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" covers the loopback callback server, history merging and filters, CoreAudio output listing, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"toolbar frame math. Tests use a separate Keychain service so they never touch the real sign-in.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Screenshots and demo mode","type":"heading","anchor":"Screenshots-and-demo-mode","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The images in these docs come from the app itself. ","type":"text"},{"code":"DOTIFY_SNAPSHOT_DIR=\/some\/dir","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" makes Dotify render every layout,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the toolbar, idle dimming, the search window and the speaker picker to 2x PNGs (see ","type":"text"},{"code":"Screenshots","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), then quit. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"restores any settings it changed.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DOTIFY_DEMO=1"},{"text":" swaps in made-up content (see ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Demo"},{"text":"): a fictional track with generated artwork, sample search","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"results and history, sample speakers, and a pretend Spotify connection. Nothing in demo mode touches Spotify, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Keychain, your saved Client ID or your listening history, so the images never show real accounts, artwork or device","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"make-screenshots.sh"},{"text":" runs both against a separate app instance and copies the PNGs into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sources\/Dotify\/Dotify.docc\/Resources","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".\/make-screenshots.sh   # refresh the images",".\/generate-docs.sh      # rebuild the docs site"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"sh"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify\/Architecture"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Dotify\/documentation\/Dotify"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfac